    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1158">

                <pb facs="1452" n="1442" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg1442"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">121.5493/4–447: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-04-04T20:00:00-05:00">April 4, 1947—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>403. War Dept expresses concern safety Rigg [and] Collins and urges consideration
                    whether any unexplored method approach might help secure their release. Dept has
                    full confidence your judgment re handling this matter but desires be in position
                    assure War Dept that all practicable steps are being taken. Accordingly if
                    current attempt utilize UNRRA<anchor n="17" xml:id="d1158-f1"/> convoy should
                    involve undue delay or bring unsatisfactory <pb facs="1453" n="1443"
                        xml:id="pg1443"/> result<anchor n="18" xml:id="d1158-f2"/> please consider
                    and report possibility other means communication with CCP.<anchor n="19"
                        xml:id="d1158-f3"/> At present no additional channels occur to us other than
                    through British should they soon despatch their Consul [to] Harbin or through
                    Soviet ConGen [at] Harbin via Soviet Embassy [in] Nanking.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1158-f1" n="17" xml:id="d1158-f1-content">
                <p>United Nations Relief and Rehabilitation Administration.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1158-f2" n="18" xml:id="d1158-f2-content">
                <p>This referred to the possibility of securing the return of the two officers by
                    means of an UNRRA truck convoy which was carrying supplies from Changchun to
                    Harbin.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1158-f3" n="19" xml:id="d1158-f3-content">
                <p>Chinese Communist Party.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
